# 13. JSON Output

The CLI should support machine-readable JSON output.

Conceptually:

```json
{
  "version": "1",
  "status": "FAIL",
  "scope": {
    "filesChecked": 8,
    "modulesChecked": 8
  },
  "summary": {
    "pass": 42,
    "warning": 3,
    "needsHumanReview": 4,
    "fail": 2
  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "example-finding-id",
      "ruleId": "CP-FM-001",
      "severity": "HARD",
      "status": "FAIL",
      "category": "frontmatter",
      "message": "Required frontmatter field 'title' is missing.",
      "file": "content/foundations/linux-fundamentals.mdx",
      "location": {
        "line": 1,
        "column": 1
      },
      "evidence": {
        "type": "metadata",
        "field": "title",
        "value": null
      },
      "remediation": "Add a non-empty 'title' field to the module frontmatter.",
      "source": {
        "type": "deterministic",
        "validator": "frontmatter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

JSON is the preferred machine-to-machine format for future GitHub integration.

