# 25. Examples by Rule Type

## Example A: Missing frontmatter

```text
FAIL
CP-FM-001
HARD
deterministic
```

Meaning:

A required field is absent.

This can block the quality gate.

---

## Example B: No em dash

```text
FAIL
CP-STYLE-004
HARD
deterministic
```

Meaning:

A prohibited em dash was detected.

The finding should point to the affected line.

---

## Example C: URL cannot be reached

```text
WARNING
CP-LINK-002
WARNING
deterministic
```

Meaning:

The URL could not be verified as reachable.

It does **not** mean the resource is inappropriate.

Resource appropriateness belongs to later semantic/human review.

---

## Example D: Technical explanation

```text
NEEDS_HUMAN_REVIEW
CP-TECH-001
HUMAN
ai_assisted
```

Meaning:

The content requires technical verification.

It does **not** mean the content is proven incorrect.

---

## Example E: Valid module relationship

```text
PASS
CP-CONSIST-001
HARD
deterministic
```

Meaning:

The relevant internal relationship passed validation.

