# 27. Acceptance Criteria

CP-AUTO-004 is complete when:

- [ ] The four result statuses are defined.
- [ ] Rule severity is separated from result status.
- [ ] Every finding has a stable CyberPivot rule ID.
- [ ] Findings identify the affected repository file.
- [ ] Findings support line/column location where available.
- [ ] Findings contain evidence.
- [ ] Findings contain actionable remediation guidance.
- [ ] Findings identify deterministic vs AI-assisted vs human provenance.
- [ ] Run-level summary counts are defined.
- [ ] Run-level status precedence is defined.
- [ ] Exit codes are defined.
- [ ] Terminal output expectations are defined.
- [ ] JSON output expectations are defined.
- [ ] CI blocking behavior is defined at a contract level.
- [ ] Contract versioning is defined.
- [ ] The contract does not claim technical accuracy can be established by simple deterministic checks.
- [ ] The contract does not introduce a new content schema.
- [ ] The contract is sufficient for CP-AUTO-005 to implement the first deterministic validator.

